# Fixed 2026-10-07, defect 458, lane b14-check.
# Symptom: `end_lease(@c, 1)` on a lease cell was told `builtin_shape`, the
# count, and `end_lease_of_no_lease`, *this argument is not such a cell*,
# which is false of `@c`: one mistake, the argument too many, and a second
# message that was not true.
# Cause: the lease rule judged the call's count again, with one message for
# every way an `end_lease` can be wrong. Now the count is the built-in
# dispatch's alone to tell.
# This case: an argument too many after the cell, before it, and a second
# cell where one is taken.

function main()
    x = "abc"
    c: cstr @= x.lease()
    end_lease(@c, 1)  #~ builtin_shape
    end_lease(1, @c)  #~ builtin_shape
    d: cstr @= x.lease()
    end_lease(@c, @d)  #~ builtin_shape
